     "sequence",
     "term",
     "rule"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A sequence is a list of numbers that follows a rule. In 3, 7, 11, 15 each term is 4 more than the one before, so the next term is 19.\nSome sequences are famous. Square numbers are 1, 4, 9, 16. Triangular numbers are 1, 3, 6, 10. The Virahanka-Fibonacci numbers are 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 where each term is the sum of the two before.\nTo describe a rule, look at the difference between terms, or at how each term is built from the earlier ones."
    }
